    Yes, for some iffy definition of "easy".  You'll have to
use a role that starts with spells, or find and successfully
read at least one spellbook.  You'll have to acquire a scroll
of amnesia.  And you'll have to get an amnesia die roll that
makes you forget at least one spell.  The formula for how
many spells to forget has changed a bit.  I don't remember
the original, other than that it added one if you were
suffering confusion at the time.  The new formula picks a
value from 0 to N (inclusive, where N is the number of
spells on your known spell list; when suffering confusion,
it makes a second roll and uses the greater of the two rolls;
there's also provision for positive luck to possibly reduce
the value chosen by the one or two rolls), so you'll need to
get a non-zero result.  The more spells you've learned, the
higher chance for that to occur.  For the more usual "I don't
want to forget my spells" case, already forgotten spells are
just as likely to be picked as castible ones, and forgetting
one which was already forgotten is effectively a no-op.


